					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:46.452207+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "u5Ch2JrJSBWVPkkmZMxlKw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "This page explains how {{gtClass:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry}} works and why it is built this way. What it is for is on the page [[Mixed subscription registry: overview]], the leak it removes on the page [[How mixing weak and strong announcement subscriptions leaks memory]]. The statements below are backed by examples in {{gtClass:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples}} or by measurements made while the registry was built."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:29:59.465975+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:57.945553+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "rWeN5ST/SsOJ0kz9pZXUKw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "| Component | Role |\n|---|---|\n| {{gtClass:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry}} | The registry: strong subscriptions in an {{gtClass:IdentitySet}}, weak ones in a separate weak part, a reentrant lock. |\n| {{gtClass:GtNoWeakSubscriptions}} / {{gtClass:GtWeakSubscriptions}} | The weak part: a stateless shared empty part, or a dictionary of one ephemeron per weak subscriber. |\n| {{gtClass:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription}} | A weak subscription: its subscriber in a one-slot {{gtClass:WeakArray}}, its action usually a {{gtClass:WeakMessageSend}}. |\n| {{gtClass:GtEphemeronSubscriptionBuilder}} | Answered by {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#weak|label=#selector}}; builds weak subscriptions. |\n| {{gtClass:GtEphemeronSubscriptionsMourner}} | The container of one ephemeron; when it is mourned it asks the registry to remove exactly that ephemeron. |\n| {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#weak}}, {{gtMethod:AnnouncementSubscription>>#makeWeak}} | GT patches that ask the announcer's registry for its weak builder, so Pharo's registries keep their exact behaviour. |\n| {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#useSubscriptionRegistry:}} | Moves an announcer, with its subscriptions, to another registry. |"
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:57.942918+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:57.942918+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "HtHPPbHHS7WAWikEG2i1ew=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Components"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:32.876002+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:34.109396+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "uTTqpLZsQkmsjhNgfaIvog=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- `strongSubscriptions`: an {{gtClass:IdentitySet}} with the strong subscriptions, as in a plain registry. Old-style {{gtClass:WeakAnnouncementSubscription}}s added to the registry are kept here too.\n- `weakSubscriptions`: the weak part. As long as there is no weak subscriber, it is {{gtClass:GtNoWeakSubscriptions}}, one stateless object shared by all registries. With the first weak subscriber it becomes a {{gtClass:GtWeakSubscriptions}} of this registry.\n- `monitor`: the reentrant {{gtClass:Mutex}} that every change and every query takes.\n- `lastChange`: a new object after every change, so that delivery notices when matching code changed the registry (decision 7)."
									}
								]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:34.104764+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:34.104764+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "B1AiMUb/SVm5XWQbaHrSvw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "An announcer holds its registry, a {{gtClass:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry}}, which has four parts:"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:45.860195+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:45.860195+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "isof08ShS9GoJIxCKG1OtQ=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- the key is the subscriber;\n- the value is an {{gtClass:IdentitySet}} with that subscriber's {{gtClass:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription}}s;\n- the container is a {{gtClass:GtEphemeronSubscriptionsMourner}}, which knows the registry and this ephemeron. When the ephemeron is mourned, it asks the registry to remove exactly this ephemeron.\n"
									}
								]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:43.52013+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:43.52013+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "dzh5IdGvQN2huvVdAPCrig=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "A {{gtClass:GtWeakSubscriptions}} holds an {{gtClass:IdentityDictionary}} with one ephemeron, a {{gtClass:WeakKeyAssociation}}, per weak subscriber. The ephemeron is itself the entry of the dictionary, so the dictionary reaches the subscriber only through the ephemeron's key:"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:47.803007+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:55.337465+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "wae8nPNVQtWZ/4JwfqOUgA=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- its subscriber weakly, through a one-slot {{gtClass:WeakArray}};\n- its action, usually a {{gtClass:WeakMessageSend}}, which references its receiver weakly, or a block, which references what it captures strongly;\n- its announcer strongly, like every Pharo subscription."
									}
								]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:55.332391+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:55.332391+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "vjpwAr+qT6+q9KVOwBH/jQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "A weak subscription, a {{gtClass:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription}}, references:"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:29:59.466004+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:47.812097+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "RADJBighRlalpi6ssExyRA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "So, unless another object holds a weak subscription itself, the only path to it goes through the announcer. Nothing global references the ephemerons: when the announcer becomes garbage, its ephemerons are garbage too and are never mourned. The mourner points at the registry, not at the weak part, so a mourn always reaches the part the registry holds at that moment."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:25.924196+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:31:25.924196+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "ZxlDEfIeSCm3FbpWjbHM6w=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# How the objects are connected"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:22.743416+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:22.743416+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "B9ZymEyTSrOGS+q0SwksFA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "1. **Subscribe.** The builder creates the subscription and the registry adds it to its subscriber's set, installing a fresh ephemeron for that subscriber ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#addWeakSubscription:}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:24.447144+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:24.447144+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "lvINIGeTTnCwt8ua6IgUCQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "2. **Deliver.** {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#deliver:}} matches the announcement under the lock, collecting only the subscriptions that handle it ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptionsHandling:}}), and delivers to them outside the lock, strong subscriptions first. The collected subscriptions do not keep their subscribers alive during the delivery, because subscriptions reference them weakly ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#weakSubscriberIsMournedByAScavengeDuringDelivery}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:26.06703+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:26.06703+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "KfJCQQzJStCY86EJd60q1g=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "3. **The subscriber dies.** At the next collection that examines it (a scavenge if it is young, a full collection if it is old) the VM fires the ephemeron, and right after the collection the finalization process mourns it: the mourner calls {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#removeEphemeron:}}, which removes the group if this ephemeron is still the current one. The subscriber itself is freed one collection later ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#firstCollectionMournsTheEntry}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:29:59.466008+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:26.073358+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "DMupyn4bRJKBgCToHDRf0Q=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "4. **Unsubscribe.** {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#removeSubscription:|label=#selector}} remove the subscription and, with the last one, the subscriber's entry. The ephemeron becomes garbage and is never mourned."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:18.809194+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:18.809194+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "1xFvYgr7S3OVoiSIsU4QAw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Life of a weak subscription"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:49.630683+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:32:49.630683+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "KWiWcEDERBqm6OAC33obOg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**1. Ephemerons held by the registry, not by the global {{gtClass:FinalizationRegistry}}.** The VM recognises an ephemeron by its class layout, not by registration; any reachable {{gtClass:WeakKeyAssociation}} whose key dies is mourned. Held inside the registry, the ephemerons are reachable only through the announcer, so a live weak subscriber cannot keep the announcer alive ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#elementOfModelIsCollectedDespiteLiveWeakSubscriber}}), removal is a dictionary operation, and a dead announcer costs no finalization work."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:33:13.365873+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:33:13.365873+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "ziHuEIU0She1gO9FrNZ67g=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**2. One ephemeron per subscriber.** The ephemeron's key is the object whose death matters, and its value is the set of that subscriber's subscriptions ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#weakSubscriptionsOfOneSubscriberShareOneEphemeron}}). This gives fewer ephemerons (about 54,000 subscriber/announcer pairs for 100,000 weak subscriptions in an image with many large Lepiter databases) and makes {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} a single lookup. It also cleans up faster: when several ephemerons share a dead key, firing one makes the key reachable again for the rest of that collection, so only one of them fires per collection; seven subscriptions of one subscriber with seven ephemerons need seven scavenges, one group needs one (see the cleanup row under Performance). The price is that delivery walks two levels, subscribers and then their subscriptions."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:33:19.529519+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:33:19.529519+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "Jtwsf7aFSou7LHhQ8cWfgw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**3. Weak subscriptions reference their subscriber weakly.** If a subscription held its subscriber strongly, anything holding the subscription, including the list of subscriptions a delivery is working through, would keep the subscriber alive, and a dying subscriber could survive scavenges and keep receiving announcements. With a {{gtClass:WeakArray}} and a {{gtClass:WeakMessageSend}}, the ephemeron is the only thing that tracks the subscriber's death."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:33:32.374829+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:33:32.374829+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "xk2BuaGUR0y/kQ8Vl4BgTw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**4. A fresh ephemeron for every weak add, removed only by identity.** A fired ephemeron cannot be reused, and its mourn can arrive late, after the subscriber was unsubscribed and subscribed again. {{gtClass:WeakKeyAssociation}}'s {{gtMethod:WeakKeyAssociation>>#mourn|label=#selector}} removes by key, so every add installs a new ephemeron, and the mourner removes an entry only while it is still that ephemeron ({{gtMethod:GtWeakSubscriptions>>#withoutEphemeron:}}, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#staleMournKeepsTheEntryOfAResubscription}}). {{gtClass:WeakKeyAssociation}}'s {{gtMethod:WeakKeyAssociation>>#mourn|label=#selector}} sends {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronSubscriptionsMourner>>#removeKey:ifAbsent:|label=#selector}} to the ephemeron's container, so a small container object, the mourner, is enough to remove exactly this ephemeron; no subclass of {{gtClass:WeakKeyAssociation}} is needed."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:34:43.952479+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:34:43.952479+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "vtV/OL+zTcaty87W5JliOA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**5. A reentrant lock.** The lock is a {{gtClass:Mutex}} because {{gtClass:BlHandlerAnnouncerRegistry}} sends {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptions|label=#selector}} inside {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#protected:|label=#selector}} ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#lockIsReentrant}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:34:48.302375+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:34:48.302375+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "BbctqijJSr+LBqu3KWjxHw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**6. Matching under the lock, as in Pharo.** Like {{gtClass:SubscriptionRegistry}}, delivery matches the announcement under the lock and collects only the subscriptions that handle it, then delivers outside the lock ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptionsHandling:}}, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#matchingHoldsTheLockAndDeliveryDoesNot}}). Only the interested subscriptions are copied, so delivery allocates no more than with a plain registry, also when subscriptions come and go between announcements. When nothing changes, a condition is evaluated as often as with a plain registry: once while matching and once more by the subscription's own {{gtMethod:AbstractAnnouncementSubscription>>#deliver:}} ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#conditionIsEvaluatedAsOftenAsInAPlainRegistry}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:29:59.46601+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:34:48.30928+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "mP/1P69ySqSSJ7EcBGOO/Q=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**7. A change marker.** Matching runs code of the subscriptions, such as {{gtMethod:Announcement class>>#where:|label=#selector}} conditions and Bloc's {{gtMethod:BlBasicEventHandler>>#wantsEvent:|label=#selector}}, and that code can change the registry while it is matched. Every change runs through {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#protectedChange:}}, which takes the lock and stores a new marker object ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#noteChange}}). When the marker changed during matching, matching is repeated on a copy of the subscriptions as they are then, so the announcement reaches exactly the subscriptions present after matching. The marker is an object rather than a counter, so registries that already exist when the code is loaded need no migration: a marker that is still nil just means no change yet. Examples:\n\n- {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#everyChangeOfTheRegistryIsNoted}}\n- {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#conditionThatChangesTheRegistryIsMatchedAgain}}\n- {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#conditionThatUnsubscribesAnotherSubscriberIsRespected}}\n- {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#whereConditionThatSubscribesDoesNotHideOtherSubscribers}}"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:07.326206+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:07.326206+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "XkEnXAaCRu6gCKGMAENySg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**8. The subscription decides its part.** {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#add:|label=#selector}} sends {{gtMethod:Object>>#addToMixedSubscriptionRegistry:|label=#selector}}; the default on {{gtClass:Object}} files any object in the strong part, so Bloc's handler subscriptions and old-style {{gtClass:WeakAnnouncementSubscription}}s keep working ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#subscriptionOfAnyClassGoesToStrongPart}}). Old-style weak subscriptions are not converted, because their global entry would remain anyway."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:22.454498+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:22.454498+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "Oco5Lo7SThmWD160dxabow=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**9. Builders own the conversions.** {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#weak|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:AnnouncementSubscription>>#makeWeak|label=#selector}} and moves between registries ask the builder of the target registry, so Pharo's registries keep their behaviour. A builder hands each new subscription to the builder of the registry its announcer uses at that moment ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#weakBuilderKeptAcrossASwitchSubscribesInTheCurrentRegistry}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:09.038647+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:22.458567+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "5H67s5Q/SpywDTd78egHlA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**10. Identity is kept where Pharo keeps it.** {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription>>#makeStrong|label=#selector}} and moves to another kind of registry {{gtMethod:ProtoObject>>#becomeForward:|label=#selector}} the old subscription to the new one, as {{gtMethod:WeakAnnouncementSubscription>>#makeStrong}} does, so references to subscriptions stay valid. {{gtMethod:AnnouncementSubscription>>#makeWeak|label=#selector}} answers a new subscription and leaves the old object as it is, as in Pharo. {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription>>#subscriber:|label=#selector}} re-files a weak subscription under the new subscriber, because helpers such as {{gtMethod:TGtWithWeakAnnouncer>>#when:send:to:for:}} set the subscriber after subscribing."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:11.677758+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:11.677758+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "IoojW9oNQWeJqed5lD5BNQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**11. Subscriptions that cannot work weakly are refused.** A nil subscriber can never be collected, and a valuable that is its own subscriber would vanish at the next collection; both signal an error, in the builder and in {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription>>#subscriber:|label=#selector}} ({{gtMethod:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription class>>#assertSubscriber:canBeWeakFor:}}). There is no weak `when:do:`; the subscriber of a weak block subscription is given with {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronSubscriptionBuilder>>#when:do:for:|label=#selector}}. A weak subscription whose subscriber is already gone, for example one added again after its subscriber was collected, is not added, because its group could never be mourned ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#weakSubscriptionWithoutSubscriberIsNotKept}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:13.17656+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:13.17656+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "6kGZRpm9R9WQx9evmE6dHw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**12. Fuel and copies.** Fuel skips the weak part, the lock and the change marker ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry class>>#fuelIgnoredInstanceVariableNames}}), so a materialized registry has only its strong subscriptions. A shallow {{gtMethod:Object>>#copy|label=#selector}} gets its own lock, a copy of the strong set and fresh ephemerons for the same weak subscriptions ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#postCopy}}, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#copiedRegistryIsIndependent}}); the subscription objects themselves are shared with the original."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:29:59.466012+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:35:13.182527+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "U/goU4ETT+2gmisP7+rYUw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**13. Read-only queries wait for the lock.** {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptions}}, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#allStrongSubscriptions}}, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#allWeakSubscriptions}}, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#weakSubscribersWithSubscriptions}} and the views copy the subscriptions under the lock ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#protected:}}). {{gtMethod:SubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptions}} answers its live set without the lock, so a reader that interrupts a change sees a half-done set: while a set grows, {{gtClass:HashedCollection}}'s {{gtMethod:HashedCollection>>#grow|label=#selector}} empties it and adds every element again. In a measurement, a process at priority 30 kept adding 5,000 subscriptions and resetting, and a process at priority 35 read all subscriptions about every millisecond. With a plain registry 496 of 1,879 reads (26 %) missed subscriptions, without any error; with the mixed registry none of 1,756 did. The price is that a query waits while another process holds the lock, for example a process stopped in the debugger inside a {{gtMethod:Announcement class>>#where:|label=#selector}} condition; deliveries, subscribing and unsubscribing wait in that case with a plain registry too. Only the size queries, {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#numberOfSubscriptions|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#isEmpty|label=#selector}}, do not take the lock, because a slightly stale count does no harm."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
