				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Concurrency"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:37:31.680835+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:37:31.680835+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "lsNitzwVRQasIz13lEGZ0g=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Measured against a plain {{gtClass:SubscriptionRegistry}}. {{gtMethod:BlockClosure>>#microsecondsToRun|label=#selector}} has only millisecond resolution in this VM, so blocks were repeated until they ran for tens of milliseconds; delivery times are the minimum of seven runs at priority 60, and allocation is the number of bytes allocated per operation.\n\n| Operation | Plain | Mixed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Weak subscription, 700 subscribers × 7, per subscription | 2.7 µs | 1.1 µs |\n| The same with unsubscribing all, per subscription | 15 µs | 1.2 µs |\n| 683 page view models created on one page and unsubscribed, per view model | 96 µs | 10 µs |\n| Strong subscribe and unsubscribe | 720 ns | 960 ns |\n| Announcement handled by 1 strong subscriber | 1.9 µs, 3.5 KB | 1.9 µs, 2.8 KB |\n| Announcement handled by 10 weak subscribers | 12.7 µs, 11.7 KB | 13.0 µs, 11.5 KB |\n| Announcement nobody handles, 100 weak subscribers | 4.4 µs, 2.7 KB | 8.0 µs, 2.4 KB |\n| Announcement handled by 1 of 1,000 weak subscribers | 46 µs, 3.7 KB | 86 µs, 3.5 KB |\n| Weak subscribe, announce, unsubscribe, announce, with 2 weak subscribers | 8.7 µs, 12.9 KB | 7.3 µs, 12.0 KB |\n| Cleanup of 700 dead young subscribers with 7 subscriptions each | 7 scavenges, 48–71 ms | 1 scavenge, 6 ms |\n\n"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:29:59.466017+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:37:31.692309+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "lROWDlM6Qgqwtq+66mNaYA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Where the differences come from:\n\n- A plain weak subscription adds an entry to the global {{gtClass:FinalizationRegistry}} (about 360 ns, under a global lock), and a plain {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} scans all subscriptions, so many elements coming and going is quadratic. The mixed registry has neither.\n- The reentrant {{gtClass:Mutex}} costs 85 ns per locked section against 40 ns for a semaphore, which shows on strong subscriptions.\n- Delivery walks the weak part under the lock, subscribers and then their sets; for large registries this walk is the expensive part (4.8 µs for 100 subscribers with one subscription each, against 0.8 µs for one flat set), which is why 100 or 1,000 weak subscribers take about twice as long as in a plain registry.\n- Delivery allocates only for the subscriptions that handle the announcement, so the mixed registry allocates no more than the plain one. The rest is the lock (about 0.5–0.8 KB per locked section) and the delivery to each subscription.\n\nMemory: an empty registry takes 184 bytes against 128; a registry's own weak part 88 bytes; a weak subscription 272 bytes for a subscriber's first and 144 bytes for each further one, against 192 bytes for a plain one with its global entry.\n\nHow these costs could be reduced is listed under \"Possible improvements\" below."
						}
					]
				},
