				},
				"string" : "# Performance"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:38:10.76838+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:38:12.986019+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "/xgwvJa1TtOtSCIzGbDx4Q=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- Between the collection that fires an ephemeron and its mourn, a dying subscriber can still receive announcements.\n- A lower-priority process that holds the registry's lock makes the finalization process wait (see Concurrency).\n- {{gtMethod:Object>>#deepCopy|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:Object>>#storeString|label=#selector}} of an announcer, a registry or a subscription recurse forever: {{gtMethod:Object>>#storeOn:|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:Object>>#deepCopy|label=#selector}} do not handle cycles, and a registry with one subscription already has one (subscription → announcer → registry). Use {{gtMethod:Object>>#copy|label=#selector}} or {{gtMethod:Object>>#veryDeepCopy|label=#selector}}."
						}
					]
				},
