										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:38.031847+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "XEobwhyWQCuJ/F7H5tC1KA=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **Store small groups without a set.** Of 19,744 weak subscriber/announcer pairs in a freshly started GT image, 59 % had one weak subscription and 37 % two (each Lepiter snippet subscribes twice to its coder). Holding the subscription itself as the ephemeron's value, or an immutable {{gtClass:Array}} for two or more, instead of a set of its own makes walking the weak part about four times cheaper (1.2 µs instead of 4.8 µs for 100 subscribers) and saves about 48–72 bytes per subscriber."
									},
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:39.429633+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:39.429633+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "TG1nlMs9SHC6B2qjR3A0dA=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **Index subscriptions by announcement class.** Delivery would look up the subscriptions of the announcement's class and its superclasses instead of matching every subscription: in a simulation 0.26 µs instead of 7.7 µs for 100 weak subscribers that nobody listens to, and 1.3 µs instead of 79 µs for 1,000. Subscriptions to announcement sets, {{gtMethod:Announcement class>>#where:|label=#selector}} conditions or symbols would need a part that is matched as today, changing a subscription's {{gtMethod:AbstractAnnouncementSubscription>>#announcementClass:|label=#selector}} would make the index stale, and every add, remove and mourn would have to keep it up to date. It only pays off for large registries, which are rare: an image with about 434,000 announcers had 29 with 101–1,000 subscriptions and 3 with more."
									},
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:15.623606+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:39.436937+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "iZvDO4tPQhK72+4rNHHcFw=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **A cached snapshot is not worth it.** Keeping a {{gtClass:WeakArray}} of all subscriptions until the next change (it must be weak, or a weak subscription whose block refers to its subscriber keeps the subscriber alive) would make delivery faster when subscriptions rarely change. But every change makes the next announcement rebuild it, so where subscriptions come and go between announcements it allocates more than matching under the lock (46 KB instead of 12 KB per subscribe, announce, unsubscribe, announce cycle with 2,000 weak subscribers, in a simulation), and every change would have to invalidate it."
									}
								]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:08.198984+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:08.198984+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "z+W33e01SxCnSHISap5IJA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Delivery**"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:40:04.130921+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:40:04.130921+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "MFJUNqheTEOVkg654xvnyg=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **Share an empty strong part** as the weak part is shared ({{gtClass:GtNoWeakSubscriptions}}): an empty registry would take 112 bytes instead of 184, less than the 128 of a plain registry. Most Lepiter snippet announcers have no subscriptions at all."
									},
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:18.556258+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:40:04.137618+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "cLsg2LXLQbmdyXgDN+lBBw=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **A cheaper lock.** The reentrant {{gtClass:Mutex}} costs 85 ns and 776 bytes of short-lived garbage per locked section, a semaphore 40 ns and 544 bytes; every announcement takes the lock once. A non-reentrant lock needs callers such as {{gtClass:BlHandlerAnnouncerRegistry}} to stop sending {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptions|label=#selector}} inside {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#protected:|label=#selector}}.\n"
									}
								]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:06.257499+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:15.64387+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "ocam+F4ST2KfyD6syL55lQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Memory and locking**"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:40:15.594122+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:40:15.594122+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "90lHn1i+TxWNq9V6ZCBNvw=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **No lost changes during a switch.** {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#basicSubscribe:|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#removeSubscription:|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} could check after the operation that the announcer's registry is still the same one and repeat the operation on the new one; repeating is harmless, because adding a subscription twice to the same registry or removing it twice changes nothing. A {{gtMethod:ProtoObject>>#becomeForward:|label=#selector}} of the old registry is not an option: a process waiting inside the old registry's method would continue that method on an object of another class."
									},
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:20.481166+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:40:15.601411+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "7RuZtnG9Tc+ste/vDXVZEA=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "- **Convert old-style weak subscriptions when moving into a mixed registry.** Their global entries would have to be removed exactly. Looking them up by key is a linear scan that can find the entry of another subscription, so a conversion should first index all global entries by their value once, then remove each with {{gtClass:FinalizationRegistry}}'s {{gtMethod:FinalizationRegistry>>#removeEphemeron:|label=#selector}}."
									}
								]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:39:28.192337+01:00"
								}
